<title>FRANCE: Elf confirms ISIS bourse intro plans.</title>
<headline>Elf confirms ISIS bourse intro plans.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Elf Aquitaine and the IFP oil institute said on Monday they planned to introduce oil services holding company ISIS on the stock exchange in the coming months.</p>
<p>Elf owns 39.1 percent of ISIS and IFP 57.3 percent, while Banque Nationale de Paris owns 3.6 percent, said a statement issued on behalf of Elf and IFP.</p>
<p>&quot;The introduction of ISIS on the Paris bourse will allow the company to diversify its shareholder structure and increase its French and international profile,&quot; they said.</p>
<p>&quot;The reduction of Elf's stake in ISIS is part of Elf's policy of focusing on core businesses,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
